  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Cambio Clim&#xe1;tico - Paisajes Sostenibles</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Landscapes and Forest Transparency Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Mexico):  With FY 2024 funds, USAID, in partnership with the U.S. Forest Service, will build the capacity of the GOM and local communities in forest management and governance to reduce deforestation and greenhouse gas emissions from the forestry sector. In particular, the new activity will work with key GOM institutions to implement an upgraded National Forest Management System to improve the transparency and legality of the harvesting and commercialization of timber and non-timber forest products. In addition, the activity will work with the GOM to implement a robust and transparent national forest inventory and monitoring system to improve forest management. This will also be used to reduce illegal logging, manage wildfires, and improve sustainable natural resource management practices. This activity will support ICS Mission Objective 3.1, related to the key issues: Sustainable Landscapes, Gender GE/WE Secondary and Partnership for Global Infrastructure Indirect..</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Cambio Clim&#xe1;tico - Paisajes Sostenibles</narrative>
  </description>
